    <TD STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Insofar
    as indemnification for liabilities arising under the Securities Act of 1933 may be permitted to directors, officers and controlling
    persons of the registrant pursuant to the foregoing provisions, or otherwise, the registrant has been advised that in the opinion
    of the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission such indemnification is against public policy as expressed in the Act and is, therefore,
